      "writtenOn": "2025-01-24T00:32:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the CL!\n\nEven the vsize copy into the writer, the AIDL interface can only pass the `Parameter.ID` to the HAL as per definition:\n```\ninterface IEffect {\n    Parameter getParameter(in Parameter.Id paramId);\n}\n```\n\nSo from the effect HAL point of view, the vsize part will not pass down, right?\nOr are you trying to address a VendorExtension use case?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 154,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 154,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "06b88c9d12214e068fa118b050cf4634dd1e18ca",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "40561087_21b624bc",
        "filename": "media/libaudiohal/impl/EffectConversionHelperAidl.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 154,
      "author": {
        "id": 3670787
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-24T14:40:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi, thanks. Yes we have a vendor effect as VendorExtension in this case. I can confirm that passing down the full size solves our use case. However I wanted to start this discussion with Google to know if this is really intended to have different behaviours on HIDL compared to AIDL with effect_param_t. I commented a bit longer in https://partnerissuetracker.corp.google.com/issues/391660114 please have a look at that.",
      "parentUuid": "1b853d4b_7a5d8978",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 154,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 154,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "06b88c9d12214e068fa118b050cf4634dd1e18ca",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cd3e1e6f_3b6b1a6d",
        "filename": "media/libaudiohal/impl/EffectConversionHelperAidl.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 154,
      "author": {
        "id": 1956242
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-28T23:14:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As mentioned in the bug: \nhttps://partnerissuetracker.corp.google.com/issues/391660114#comment7\n\nIf only psize is append to the cmd buffer, then I think we will get a OOB memory access with the memcpy in the CL (pCmdData does not have a valid vsize part)\n\nIt might be okay for your case if passing directly to audioserver, but this change will break other use cases from libaudioclient.\nI suggest we abandon this change, and investigate other approaches like \"pass it as part of the parameter (psize of effect_param_t)\".\nThanks!",
      "parentUuid": "40561087_21b624bc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 154,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 154,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "06b88c9d12214e068fa118b050cf4634dd1e18ca",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
